A||||8||Homicidal||Does anybody know the Wattage handeling of the STOCK 4X10's?||||5||
Z||000000||Homicidal||06-20-2000||07:10 PM||||I am thinking of bidding on these if they are more powerful than what I have.<P>Just a quicky question:  How does the RMS handeling differ from the peak?<BR> <A HREF="http://cgi.ebay.com/aw-cgi/eBayISAPI.dll?ViewItem&item=361082538" TARGET=_blank>http://cgi.ebay.com/aw-cgi/eBayISAPI.dll?ViewItem&item=361082538</A> ||||reg||5
Z||000001||ThatRickGuy||06-20-2000||07:46 PM||||yes, RMS is the important number, the peek means that it can take a blast of 105 watts with out shooting the cone out of the magnet for the most part, but it you try pushing 105 watts threw that thing constantly, you'll have confeti in no time. 35 watts rms is probrably better then the stock speakers, definately better then 12-16 year old stock speakers. it would probrably work well with the sony or pioneer 40 watt head units, turning it up all the way would definately distort the sound, but you'd get good quality from it up to about 1/2 crank. The only other thing is, (maybe I'm wrong on this) but aren't the dash speakers in a fiero 4x9s?||||reg||1
Z||000002||stimpy||06-20-2000||08:14 PM||||I have a set of these in my car. I will be replacing them w/Kenwoods or Pioneers, but they are an improvement over stock, if only because they use more modern materials.||||reg||1
Z||000003||theogre||06-20-2000||10:46 PM||||I wouldn't waste any time at all on the stock speakers. Even cheap replacements will be better. I've got some cheap Ecilpse coaxials in the front. They sound pretty good. They are good for like 40-50w continuous I think.<P>Generally you don't want or need allot of power in the front or the sail speakers. Has a nasty habit of making surounding parts rattle and buzz like hell. The speaker grills themselves aren't exactly the most rugged things either. I rattled chunks out of one of mine, and that was just running it with the factory radio.<P>Main thing you want in the front speakers is something that can take increadible heat. My eclipse for example came partly unglued around the edges from the heat of sunlight on the dash. The cones and all are good, but the glue came loose that holds the surounds to the frames.<p>[This message has been edited by theogre (edited 06-20-2000).]||||reg||1
Z||000004||Monkeyman||06-20-2000||11:07 PM||||Rick--4x10s.  Never heard of 4x9s.||||reg||1
Z||000005||1FST2M6||06-20-2000||11:24 PM||||BlackGT and I just installed a new radio and front speakers in his car this afternoon...  after some not so bright ex-owner THRASHED the wiring harness and i straightened that out I'm used to haveing my 2 sets of 4" up front and 10 in the floor.. his 86GT with with these 4x10s really didn't sound to bad! decent extension and really clear! Kenwood 2way not sure of the model # but I was impressed... can't get clear sound out of an oval speaker but this is REALLY close.||||reg||1
Z||000006||Standard||06-20-2000||11:29 PM||||I have pioneer 2 ways all around, and I just installed a pioneer deck (22 watts RMS, 45 watts max) and I think it sounds really nice.  Pretty clear, tho not the best bass.  I hope to change that soon...||||reg||1
Z||000007||Oreif||06-21-2000||02:39 AM||||Most standard GM radios are 12W max output. Of course this is rated into a 10 ohm speaker! GM is vary weird with speakers. Some are 10 ohms some are 6 ohms and some newer ones are 4 ohms (4 ohms being the car audio standard) The Fieros fit in the 6 ohm catagory. The stock paper cones are good for 10W after that the paper tends to distort rapidly. Any aftermarket speaker will sound better with an aftermarket stereo. The GM radios with aftermarket speakers will sound better and low volume but will still distort easily due to impedence mismatch of the radios amplifier section. You can get around this by using an aftermarket amp that has a "high level input section". Stock radio output to amp input, Amp output to speakers. Most aftermarket amps have an impedence matching circuit to correct this.  GM speakers with aftermarket radio will sound "dull" the mid and high freq's get lost due to the thicker voice coil wire in stock GM speakers (reason the ohms are different).<BR>Hope this helps! ||||reg||1
Z||000008||lou_dias||06-21-2000||09:46 AM||||I have a CD player/radio from a 98 Blazer in my 87GT with Jenson 10x4's from Crutchfield in the front and it sounds pretty damn good!  Hopefully this weekend, I will be putting in Kenwoods 4x6's to replace the factory sails and finally put in the amp and harness to the factory subwoofer system that I added.  That 98 Blazer unit really puts out alot of power!  And the bass through the Jensen's is pretty decent!  The quality of the radio receiver leaves alot to be desired compared to playing a CD, but maybe I'm just spoiled now.||||reg||1
